{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuTK9HftNnXiyQrFtsFa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard or check that the rule's query matches any documents.\n\n**Fields:** The data view has `timestamp`, `response` (a string with a `.keyword` subfield), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url` and `request`, among others.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-7525b2bf Web logs overview\" has four panels, with a default range of the last 7 days:\n- **Total requests:** a single-number count.\n- **Requests over time:** a line chart of request counts.\n- **Requests by response code:** a pie chart of the top 10 `response.keyword` values.\n- **Average bytes by extension:** a bar chart of average `bytes` per file extension.\n\nYou can open it at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-7525b2bf-web-logs-overview-dc5ec1f354c4.\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-7525b2bf 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- **Schedule:** it runs every minute.\n- **Condition:** it fires when more than 10 documents match `response.keyword: 5*` in the last 5 minutes.\n- **Enabled:** it was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n- **No actions:** it has none attached, so a firing will show up in Kibana but won't notify anyone.\n\nThe sample data has fixed timestamps, so the rule may rarely or never fire unless new 5xx documents arrive."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":960,"cache_read_input_tokens":20316,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":960},"output_tokens":532,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0536cbf5-c97a-5467-80bd-e50c5d30a2